    "body": "Just checking in; what's the latest status on this PR, and is the OP up to date in that regard? In particular:\r\n\r\n- The OP says that both Mozilla and Chromium support this change, but https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/339 contains some debate, and [the blink-dev thread](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!topic/blink-dev/7nHTRUP1EGY) does not have any positive responses at the moment.\r\n\r\n- The OP links to https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/webappapis/system-state-and-capabilities/the-navigator-object/protocol.https.html and has the \"tests are written\" box checked, but none of the protocols added in this PR are tested in that file.\r\n\r\n- @annevk desires that everything we add be IANA registered. I know you've been doing a lot of this work, but also the list keeps expanding, so I'm not 100% sure if everything in the PR is registered. Could you confirm?\r\n\r\nAgain, thanks for driving this forward; I'm really hopeful you'll succeed where others have failed. I'm excited to merge this as soon as possible, but the information in the OP is a bit confusing for me right now.",
